<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Landsgemeinde</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Landsgemeinde is the open-air assembly of all qualified citizens of a Swiss canton or district, meeting once a year to elect officials and vote on laws by show of hands. It governed the rural cantons of central and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> and is one of the oldest forms of direct democracy. Today it survives at cantonal level only in Appenzell Innerrhoden and Glarus.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/landsgemeinde.jpg" alt="Landsgemeinde" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marc Schlumpf, www.icarus-design.ch · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Landsgemeinde_Glarus,_2009.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
